From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Flax <hmccanne@exclamationpoint.com>
Date: Mon, 27 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] user_mgr: allow hyphen in usernames (HI-FW host interface)

The AMI Redfish Host Interface firmware account is named "HI-FW" (fixed by
the TP26 BIOS, which authenticates its inventory push as that user). AMI
patch 0025 set the username validation regex to ^[a-zA-Z0-9_.*]{1,16}$,
which forbids the hyphen, so CreateUser("HI-FW") fails with
"Invalid username" and the account can never be provisioned. Add '-' to the
allowed character class so the host-interface account can be created.

Signed-off-by: Flax <hmccanne@exclamationpoint.com>
---
--- a/user_mgr.cpp
+++ b/user_mgr.cpp
@@ -319,7 +319,7 @@
                               Argument::ARGUMENT_VALUE("Invalid length"));
     }
     if (!std::regex_match(userName.c_str(),
-                          std::regex("^[a-zA-Z0-9_.*]{1,16}$")))
+                          std::regex("^[a-zA-Z0-9_.*-]{1,16}$")))
     {
         lg2::error("Invalid username '{USERNAME}'", "USERNAME", userName);
         elog<InvalidArgument>(Argument::ARGUMENT_NAME("User name"),
